---
// Approach / doctrine section — ported from the landing design handoff
---

<section style="position:relative;z-index:1;border-top:1px solid rgba(240,240,220,.06);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,240,220,.06);background:linear-gradient(180deg,#1d1d1a,#1a1a18);">
  <div class="gw-section-pad" style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 32px;">
    <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#26c87d;">The approach</div>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(28px,3.6vw,42px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:14px 0 0;max-width:20ch;">Do one thing well. Compose with everything.</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#b4b4ac;margin:18px 0 0;max-width:52ch;">An interrupt pauses one workflow inside one framework. Gatewerk is the review layer across all of them: one inbox, one record, any stack.</p>

    <div class="gw-approach-grid">
      <div class="gw-approach-col">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#7b7b72;">01</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:#f7f7f1;margin:16px 0 0;">Primitives, not opinions</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#9a9a8f;margin:11px 0 0;">Gatewerk fires events and exposes an API. You wire it to Telegram, Slack, or your own service and decide what gets reviewed. A notification channel is a settings entry, not a project. No workflow is baked in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gw-approach-col">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#7b7b72;">02</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:#f7f7f1;margin:16px 0 0;">Strength in the substrate</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#9a9a8f;margin:11px 0 0;">The guarantees hold at the database and worker layer, not by convention. They stay invisible until the moment they save you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gw-approach-col">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#7b7b72;">03</div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:#f7f7f1;margin:16px 0 0;">Open protocol, your infrastructure</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#9a9a8f;margin:11px 0 0;">Built on the Human Review Protocol. Self hosted, AGPL, no vendor lock in, no feature behind a sales call.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="font-family:'Bricolage Grotesque',sans-serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(17px,2vw,21px);line-height:1.4;color:#cfcfc5;margin:40px 0 0;max-width:36ch;">Built once, properly, so you don't have to build the fourth dashboard.</p>
  </div>
</section>
